verdicts.evidence:
Reproduced in both builds. The books are worse than both 9297d2d and 56dfd93, not owner-accepted (Left (1) still waits on the owner), and were already lost at b666461 (e7ca679's 0 Tw), not in 935b077.

he `p { letter-spacing: 0.3em; word-spacing: -0.2em }` `<p>שלום.<br/>בראשית (אלהים).</p>`, default build:
- 9297d2d c1l1 `שלום. | בראשית (אלהים) | .`;
- 56dfd93 c1l1;
- b666461 c0l0;
- tip c0l0 `שלום. | .בראשית (אלהים)`.
Content streams: at 9297d2d and 56dfd93, Bx0 is written at -2.4 Tw, which moved the glyphs after code 32 (א ר ב) 2.4pt left. That left a 6pt (0.5em) gap before the stop, and the stop was read alone. At the tip Bx0 is at 0 Tw, the gap is 3.6pt, and the stop joins the run.
The comma tie-break's shape needs the leftmost unit to be R or AL (bidi.rs:603). The line's leftmost glyph is `)` at x=42, so the line is read right to left and the stop comes first.
READINGS_PER_LINE=1e6 and no-pieces fix none of these books, which agrees with 'no drawing tried reads it right'.

Same pattern (c1l1 at both baselines, c0l0 at the tip), default build:
- units styled/none, he and ar, at ls 0.15/ws 0.3 and ls 0.3/ws -0.2;
- transform styled/none he at none, scaleX(0.5), scaleX(0.7), translateX(12px) and line-height 0.4;
- transform ar at scaleX(0.5) and scaleX(0.7).
Bundled-fonts:
- ar units ×2 and ar transform scaleX(0.5) and (0.7) go c1l1 → c0l0;
- at the baselines these drew a visible overlap (ov x/1), except ls 0.3/ws -0.2 (ov 1/0);
- the he books are c0 at every tree.

Corrections:
- br-num-ws5 is at ws 0.5em, which is Left (1)'s own named spacing. Only the ls 0.15/ws 0.3 cut is a spacing Left (1) does not name.
- The root is Left (1)'s tie-break. Until the owner rules, the action is to name the closing-bracket left end and the bundled-fonts Arabic books in ROADMAP CD-19 and epub.md, with counts.

